  "notes": [
    "This is an editorial primary-role display taxonomy, not a new corpus extraction, a legal status register, an affiliation claim or an importance ranking. Original measured classes and source records remain unchanged.",
    "Every named actor has exactly one primary colour. Named people can share a role colour with an institution or field without being treated as organisations. Named corporate buyers represent the legal-department role discussed in the corpus, not their entire business.",
    "The ten strategic group IDs and their full names are retained. A group-level relationship does not automatically apply to each named member; a named actor’s secondary display role does not add a relationship.",
    "Related groups deliberately share the existing fourteen colour families. Diamond labels and group descriptions identify the exact constituency; matching colour alone is not proof of identical membership.",
    "A-16 and A-23 have no named members in this retained actor inventory. Their collective diamonds remain analytically useful in the strategic core without inventing named representatives.",
    "Harvard Business School is primarily research and scholarship; Harvard Law School is primarily legal education with research as an additional role. The wider research group includes economics, management, computer science and law.",
    "AI-native legal services retain the existing six named historical/current providers. Product vendors such as Harvey, Legora, EvenUp and Ironclad stay in legal technology. Atrium remains a historical case, not an assertion that it still operates."
